# No unsolicited git

He keeps editorial control of the tree. Write and edit files. Then stop.

- Do **not** run `git add`, `git commit`, or `git push` unless he explicitly asks in that turn.
- "So I can run it", "fix this", "on the box", or finishing a feature is **not** a commit request.
- Do not stage "while you're here" extras. Leave everything unstaged for him to review.
- If he asks you to commit, add only the paths he named (or the files from that request). Show him the status first if anything else is dirty.
- Never `git add -A` / `git add .` unless he said to include everything.
